Z||000000||mrtgman||09-02-2001||12:28 AM||||Hi all,<P>I am looking for suggestions as to the brightest shade of red to paint my 86GT. I have looked on chevys site for the new corvette colors and also pontiacs for the trans am red. Both look pretty good. Any ideas or comments on where to find a great shade of red for my car?<P>Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rick 88||09-02-2001||02:08 AM||||Here are two reds to check out. In 75 Trans Am's came in Buccaneer Red. It's a nice bright red. In 76 Trans Am's came in Carrousel Red. It is actually a red-orange color. It is very nice. I used it on a V8 Vega and got lots of compliments way back then. <P>Rick<BR>yellow 88 GT 5-speed||||reg||3
Z||000002||Leper||09-02-2001||02:11 AM||||Try looking on <A HREF="http://www.paintscratch.com/search.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.paintscratch.com/search.htm</A> <BR>here's some bright red colors that i've found<BR>since you can't see them all at one time due to the differences in names, here's a list so you can compare yourself.<P>Acura New Formula Red, code:  R-510 (NSX color)<BR>AMC Flash red perl metallic clearcoat, code: cv (From an 88 Alliance of all things, but it's pretty bright)<BR>AMG Candy Apple Red. code:  R19 <BR>Buick Torch Red, code: 70/WA9075 <BR>Cadillac Flame red, code: 74/WA8748 <BR>Daewoo Super Red, code: 73L (so far i think it's the brightest)<BR>Hyundai Cardinal red, code: PU <BR>Isuzu Palazzo red clearcoat, code: 806/R902 <BR>Jaguar Bright red/Signal red, code: 748/CFC <BR>Land Rover Monza Red Clearcoat, code:  LRC590/CCZ <BR>Peugeot Italian Red, code:  PKB <BR>Plymouth Prowler red, code: RD/VRD <BR>newer Porsche Guards red, code:  80K/G1 84A <BR>VW flash red, code:  LP3G/D8 <BR>||||reg||1
